 expert ratings.", "Incumbent Tony Wied (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Tony Wied, a Republican freshman, seeks a second term in Wisconsin's 8th District, a northeastern Wisconsin seat that leaned about eight points Republican at the presidential level. He faces Democrat Rick Crosson, whose military ties are central to his campaign and who has pressed ethics themes. Wied has raised roughly $1.35 million to Crosson's $168,000 and holds a wide cash advantage heading into the final stretch.\n\nEvery major race rating published this fall places the district on the Republican side, with six outlets calling it Safe or Solid Republican and four calling it Likely Republican. Prediction markets give Crosson roughly a one-in-ten chance. The race has drawn local debates and coverage of Wied's stock trades, but no public polls have measured the contest, leaving the national midterm environment as the main unknown.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0582, "margin": -10.2}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.052, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.066, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0699, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.033, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0472, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0442, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0408, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0357, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0325, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0408, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0417, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0896, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0338, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0493, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0504, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0382, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0285, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_de